# Press releases of the Swiss federal administration, German edition.
# Published by the Federal Chancellery and the departments, set to the
# Chancellery house standard: Swiss guillemets, no eszett.
# region: <main id="main-content">
#
# 36 of these were frozen from the two admin.ch listings on 2026-08-09, one of
# which the publisher later withdrew and which was dropped. The other 119 were
# taken on 2026-08-15 from the Internet Archive's index of the same publisher's
# German newsroom, in URL order and blind to what any of them says. That last
# part is the load-bearing one: this corpus exists to carry Swiss guillemets, and
# picking press releases by whether they quote anything would make the guillemet
# count a property of the picking rather than of how the Chancellery writes.
#
# A second column is an Internet Archive capture: fixed bytes, so a rebuild
# reproduces instead of resampling. A URL without one is fetched live, and
# `--live` ignores the column entirely. gates/README.md has the coverage.
